Thanks for reaching out! The issue isn't that the beta header has expired — it's still a valid value (`prompt-caching-2024-07-31`) and can be included if desired. However, **sending the beta header alone does not enable prompt caching**. You also need to include a `cache_control` parameter in your request body.

Prompt caching requires one of two approaches in your request payload:

**Option 1 — Automatic caching (recommended):** Add a top-level `cache_control` field:
```json
{
  "model": "claude-3.5-sonnet-20241022",
  "max_tokens": 1024,
  "cache_control": { "type": "ephemeral" },
  "system": "your system prompt here...",
  "messages": [...]
}
```

**Option 2 — Explicit cache breakpoints:** Place `cache_control` directly on the content block(s) you want cached:
```json
{
  "model": "claude-3.5-sonnet-20241022",
  "max_tokens": 1024,
  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "your long prompt prefix...",
          "cache_control": { "type": "ephemeral" }
        }
      ]
    },
    ...
  ]
}
```

Once caching is enabled this way, and the same prefix is reused within the cache TTL (default 5 minutes), subsequent responses will include `cache_creation_input_tokens` (first use) or `cache_read_input_tokens` (subsequent hits) alongside `input_tokens` and `output_tokens`.

Note that `cache_control` is supported natively on the standard Messages API endpoint (`POST /v1/messages`) — no beta header is required. See our [Prompt Caching guide](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/prompt-caching) for full details and examples.

Also note: your SDK version (`@anthropic-ai/sdk@0.24.0`) should support `cache_control` on message content blocks. If you're constructing requests manually, double-check that the `cache_control` field is being serialized into the JSON body correctly.
